WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.813
An AI system's identity isn't the model.

2
00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:06.549
It's the software around it,
sorted by whose token it presents.

3
00:00:06.549 --> 00:00:10.112
A signed-in user's, so it can
do everything that user can.

4
00:00:10.112 --> 00:00:13.066
Its own, as a workload or agent identity,

5
00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:16.850
where today the only policy
control is to block it.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.138
Or no token at all, just a key.

7
00:00:19.138 --> 00:00:25.069
Microsoft's agent identity platform
became generally available in April 2026,

8
00:00:25.069 --> 00:00:29.922
but the agent policies are still
preview, G C C has a partial subset,

9
00:00:29.922 --> 00:00:33.787
and GCC High and DoD have
no published availability.

10
00:00:33.787 --> 00:00:37.588
And licensing governance for people
doesn't license it for agents.

11
00:00:37.588 --> 00:00:41.131
So the CIO budgets the
licenses, and every capability

12
00:00:41.131 --> 00:00:44.900
is confirmed in your own cloud
before anyone plans on it.
